From: Beaverfffan <Beaverfffan@users.noreply.github.com>
Subject: ath12k: give the GL-BE3600 a settle window before the first START_AP

netifd and hostapd are already waiting when the phy appears on this board,
so START_AP can land ~300 ms after the firmware reports ready.  The
firmware accepts the vdev but never puts a beacon on the air, while
hostapd still logs AP-ENABLED and the interface stays bridged, which looks
exactly like a missing signal.  Leaving a few seconds between the phy
appearing and the first START_AP avoids it (measured: 0.3 s silent,
5.3 s beacons), so delay the registration on this machine only.

Signed-off-by: Beaverfffan <Beaverfffan@users.noreply.github.com>

--- a/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath12k/core.c
+++ b/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath12k/core.c
@@ -5,6 +5,7 @@
  */
 
 #include <linux/export.h>
+#include <linux/delay.h>
 #include <linux/module.h>
 #include <linux/slab.h>
 #include <linux/remoteproc.h>
@@ -1252,6 +1253,17 @@
 	if (WARN_ON(ret))
 		goto err_mac_destroy;
 
+	/* The GL-BE3600 comes up with netifd and hostapd already waiting for
+	 * the phy, so START_AP can land ~300 ms after the firmware reports
+	 * ready.  On this board the firmware then accepts the vdev but never
+	 * puts a beacon on the air, while hostapd still logs AP-ENABLED and
+	 * the interface stays bridged - it looks exactly like a missing
+	 * signal.  Leaving a gap between the phy appearing and the first
+	 * START_AP avoids it (measured: 0.3 s silent, 5.3 s beacons).
+	 */
+	if (of_machine_is_compatible("gl.inet,gl-be3600"))
+		msleep(6000);
+
 	ret = ath12k_mac_register(ag);
 	if (WARN_ON(ret))
 		goto err_mlo_teardown;
